@startuml FileRelicImplementedArchitecture
title FileRelic — Current Implementation (reference-diagram layout)

left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #334155
  ArrowColor #475569
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #94A3B8
}

legend bottom
  Solid boxes are C++ classes or structs that exist in the code.
  Boxes marked «free functions» group real functions; they are not classes.
  This diagram follows the supplied class.jpeg's left-to-right flow while
  describing the current implementation, including its present CLI-based GUI link.
endlegend

package "User interface" {
  class "CLI entry point" as CliMain <<function>> {
    +main(argc, argv)
    +dispatch help / version / inspect / demo
  }

  class MainWindow <<Qt class>> {
    +chooseImage()
    +analyzeImage()
    +appendOutput()
    +inspectionFinished(exitCode, exitStatus)
    +toggleRawLog(visible)
    -cliPath(): QString
    -inspectImage(path)
    -renderResults(succeeded)
    -clearResults()
    -addResultCard(...)
    -selectedImagePath: QString
    -rawReport: QString
  }
  class QProcess <<Qt class>>
}

package "Image inspection" {
  class "Partition table functions" as PartitionFunctions <<free functions>> {
    inspect_image_file(path)
    inspect_mbr(image, size)
    inspect_extended_partition(...)
    inspect_gpt(image, size)
    read_gpt_header(...)
    read_partition_entry(...)
  }

  class "Filesystem functions" as FilesystemFunctions <<free functions>> {
    detect_file_system(...)
    print_file_system_report(...)
    inspect_ext_superblock(...)
    inspect_ext_root_directory(...)
    inspect_ext_file_inode(...)
  }

  class "Binary and image helpers" as BinaryFunctions <<free functions>> {
    read_sector(...)
    read_bytes_at(...)
    matches_bytes_at(...)
    read_little_endian_u32(...)
    read_little_endian_u64(...)
    crc32_ieee(...)
    read_ascii_field(...)
    format_uuid(...)
  }

  class MbrEntry <<struct>> {
    +type: unsigned char
    +start_sector: uint32
    +sector_count: uint32
  }

  class GptHeader <<struct>> {
    +header_size: uint32
    +current_lba: uint64
    +backup_lba: uint64
    +first_usable_lba: uint64
    +last_usable_lba: uint64
    +partition_entries_lba: uint64
    +partition_entry_count: uint32
    +partition_entry_size: uint32
    +partition_entries_crc32: uint32
  }

  class ExtSuperblockInfo <<struct>> {
    +block_size: uint32
    +inode_size: uint16
    +inodes_per_group: uint32
  }
}

package "Report and output" {
  class InspectionReport <<struct>> {
    +image_path: filesystem::path
    +image_size_bytes: uintmax_t
    +exit_code: int
    +rendered_text: string
    +succeeded(): bool
  }

  class "Inspection API" as InspectApi <<free function>> {
    +inspect_image(path): InspectionReport
  }

  class "Report rendering API" as RenderApi <<free function>> {
    +render_report(report, output)
  }
}

package "External framework" {
  class "Qt Widgets" as QtWidgets <<framework>>
  class "filerelic executable" as CliExecutable <<process>>
}

CliMain --> InspectApi : inspect command
CliMain --> PartitionFunctions : demo fixtures
InspectApi --> PartitionFunctions : performs inspection
PartitionFunctions --> FilesystemFunctions : detects filesystem
PartitionFunctions --> BinaryFunctions : reads and validates bytes
FilesystemFunctions --> BinaryFunctions : decodes metadata
PartitionFunctions --> MbrEntry : reads entries
PartitionFunctions --> GptHeader : validates headers
FilesystemFunctions --> ExtSuperblockInfo : fills metadata
InspectApi --> InspectionReport : returns
RenderApi --> InspectionReport : formats
MainWindow --> QProcess : starts process
QProcess --> CliExecutable : launches
MainWindow --> QtWidgets : builds result cards
CliExecutable ..> CliMain : runs

note bottom of MainWindow
  The GUI currently invokes the CLI and presents its output as readable cards.
  It does not consume InspectionReport directly yet.
end note

note bottom of InspectionReport
  This shared report currently stores image status and rendered text.
  Typed partition and filesystem result collections are future work.
end note

@enduml
